From: VyOS LS1046A <build@vyos.io>
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: skip dpaa_eth_init_ports for proxy children

fsl_dpa calls dpaa_eth_init_ports() which creates FMan PCD schemes
(RSS) for all ports. When dpa_app later calls fmc_execute() to push
CDX offload schemes, FM_PCD_KgSchemeSet() fails with "Resource
Already Exists — Scheme id (0)" because the kernel already created
schemes at those IDs.

Fix: skip dpaa_eth_init_ports() for proxy children (parent compatible
"fsl,dpa-ethernet-init"). dpa_app configures FMan PCD for these ports
via CDX at runtime. For direct children (eth0-2 RJ45), keep existing
behavior (kernel RSS).

A follow-up sed patch in auto-build.yml also skips RX PCD scheme
creation for ALL ports by inserting a return in dpaa_eth_init_rx_port().

Side effect: proxy-child ports (eth3/eth4) won't pass RX traffic
until dpa_app successfully programs the FMan PCD (~T+64s at boot).

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
@@ -1068,9 +1068,14 @@ dpaa_eth_priv_probe(struct platform_device *_of_dev)
 	priv->tx_headroom = dpa_get_headroom(&priv->buf_layout[TX]);
 	priv->rx_headroom = dpa_get_headroom(&priv->buf_layout[RX]);
 
-	/* All real interfaces need their ports initialized */
-	dpaa_eth_init_ports(mac_dev, dpa_bp, count, &port_fqs,
-			buf_layout, dev);
+	/* All real interfaces need their ports initialized.
+	 * Proxy children skip port init — dpa_app configures
+	 * FMan PCD for these ports via CDX at runtime.
+	 */
+	if (!of_device_is_compatible(dpa_node->parent,
+				"fsl,dpa-ethernet-init"))
+		dpaa_eth_init_ports(mac_dev, dpa_bp, count,
+				&port_fqs, buf_layout, dev);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_FMAN_PFC
 	for (i = 0; i < CONFIG_FMAN_PFC_COS_COUNT; i++) {
